# vehje-runtime-driver, known gaps

## std-feature

The crate root is a hardcoded `#![no_std]`, so the current type and
dispatch surface is genuinely no_std. A default `std` cargo feature
is reserved for the dylib-loading path (opening the Zig runtime dylib
through `std::fs` and, later, `libloading`), which needs std; that
path is not yet wired, so the feature currently gates nothing live.
The no_std-only build is the embedded-target future where dylib
dispatch is replaced with statically linked extension slots. This
entry replaces the earlier stale note that described a
`cfg_attr(not(feature = "std"), no_std)` shape the crate no longer
uses; the crate moved to literal `#![no_std]`.
